BLUETTI Local Wi-Fi

Derived in part from BLUETTI Integration for Home Assistant 1.0.5:
https://github.com/bluetti-official/bluetti-home-assistant
Copyright (c) 2025 Bluetti. Distributed under the MIT license in LICENSE.

The official BluettiState/BluettiDevice callback model, numeric sensor structure,
function codes and icon mapping are adapted in models.py, sensor.py,
binary_sensor.py, const.py and icon_config.py. Source hashes are recorded in
provenance.json. The local edition uses a distinct bluetti_local integration domain.

The read-only EL30V2 Wi-Fi transport, register decoder, local configuration flow,
freshness checks and tests are modifications/additions by the BLUETTI Local Wi-Fi
contributors, distributed under the same MIT license.

Background protocol research for a different device, the AC300:
https://tvdr.de/bluetti-monitor/
The EL30V2 framing, register mapping and direct MQTT handshake were independently
validated with an owner's device. No code from that AC300 implementation is included.

EL30V2 readable register addresses, formats and enum values were cross-checked
with the MIT-licensed bluetti-bt-lib model profile:
https://github.com/Patrick762/bluetti-bt-lib/blob/main/bluetti_bt_lib/devices/el30v2.py
The local profile decoder/discovery implementation is independent; no reference
classes are copied and no Bluetooth library is required at runtime.
